## 4. Criar a função `DenySecPolicies`

- [ ] `law-security` → **Logs** → colar a query → **Save → Save as function** → Nome `DenySecPolicies` · Categoria `Security`
- [ ] Testar: `DenySecPolicies | where TimeGenerated > ago(1d) | take 10`

### 4.1. Com nome da subscription

```kusto
AzureActivity
| where OperationNameValue =~ "Microsoft.Authorization/policies/deny/action"
| extend p = parse_json(tostring(Properties_d.policies))
| mv-expand p
| extend AssignmentScope = tolower(tostring(p.policyAssignmentScope))
| project
    DateTime       = datetime_utc_to_local(TimeGenerated, "America/Sao_Paulo"),
    TimeGenerated,
    SubscriptionId = tolower(SubscriptionId),
    SubscriptionMG = tostring(split(tostring(Properties_d.ancestors), ",")[0]),
    ResourceGroup  = tolower(ResourceGroup),
    Resource       = tostring(Properties_d.resource),
    ResourceType   = tostring(Properties_d.resourceProviderValue),
    Location       = tostring(Properties_d.resourceLocation),
    Initiative     = coalesce(tostring(p.policySetDefinitionDisplayName), "(standalone policy)"),
    Policy         = tostring(p.policyDefinitionDisplayName),
    Assignment     = tostring(p.policyAssignmentDisplayName),
    AssignmentName = tostring(p.policyAssignmentName),
    AssignmentMG   = extract(@"managementgroups/([^/]+)", 1, AssignmentScope),
    AssignmentScope,
    Caller,
    CallerIpAddress,
    CorrelationId
| join kind=leftouter hint.remote=left (
    arg("").ResourceContainers
    | where type == "microsoft.resources/subscriptions"
    | project SubscriptionId = tolower(subscriptionId), SubscriptionName = name
  ) on SubscriptionId
| project-away SubscriptionId1
| project-reorder DateTime, SubscriptionName, SubscriptionId
```

### 4.2. Sem nome da subscription (sem `arg()`)

Usar quando o `arg()` não estiver disponível ou quem consulta não tiver Reader nas subscriptions. A coluna `SubscriptionName` recebe o ID para manter as consultas compatíveis.

```kusto
AzureActivity
| where OperationNameValue =~ "Microsoft.Authorization/policies/deny/action"
| extend p = parse_json(tostring(Properties_d.policies))
| mv-expand p
| extend AssignmentScope = tolower(tostring(p.policyAssignmentScope))
| project
    DateTime       = datetime_utc_to_local(TimeGenerated, "America/Sao_Paulo"),
    TimeGenerated,
    SubscriptionId = tolower(SubscriptionId),
    SubscriptionMG = tostring(split(tostring(Properties_d.ancestors), ",")[0]),
    ResourceGroup  = tolower(ResourceGroup),
    Resource       = tostring(Properties_d.resource),
    ResourceType   = tostring(Properties_d.resourceProviderValue),
    Location       = tostring(Properties_d.resourceLocation),
    Initiative     = coalesce(tostring(p.policySetDefinitionDisplayName), "(standalone policy)"),
    Policy         = tostring(p.policyDefinitionDisplayName),
    Assignment     = tostring(p.policyAssignmentDisplayName),
    AssignmentName = tostring(p.policyAssignmentName),
    AssignmentMG   = extract(@"managementgroups/([^/]+)", 1, AssignmentScope),
    AssignmentScope,
    Caller,
    CallerIpAddress,
    CorrelationId
| extend SubscriptionName = SubscriptionId   // sem arg(): usa o ID no lugar do nome
| project-reorder DateTime, SubscriptionName, SubscriptionId
```

Regras de uso:

- Uma linha **por policy** que bloqueou → contar deploys com `dcount(CorrelationId)`.
- Excluir assignments da plataforma: `| where not(AssignmentName startswith "sys.")`.

